# Phase 11: two processes exchange 100,000 messages through a port in order
# with none lost; the kernel identifies the peer; a protected port refuses a
# process without permission; a file and shared memory cross a port; a
# futex-based mutex in shared memory keeps a counter exact across 4 processes.
cerberus kernel shell
!send run /bin/ipctest
!wait 30
100000 messages through a port, in order, none lost
the kernel identified the peer as pid
a closed peer gives EPIPE, a closed port ENOENT
uid 1000 was refused by a 0600 port (EACCES) and accepted by a 0666 one
a file and 64 KiB of shared memory crossed a port; both sides saw each other's writes
4 processes added 50000 each under a futex mutex: the counter is exactly 200000
a full queue made the sender wait (and port_try_send gave EAGAIN); nothing was lost or reordered
ipctest: PASS
run: /bin/ipctest exited with status 0
